  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Christian Youth Training Centre CCJ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enable disadvantaged young people in poor areas of Sao Paulo and Brazil to engage with and contribute to the strengthening of civil society as an effective strategy to develop long-term solutions to social problems faced by youth (such as violence, corruption, lack of housing, employment, precarious health and education). 
This two-year project will be implemented by local partner CCJ. It will build on the work, lessons learnt and impact of the European Community funded Urban Livelihoods programme (2008-2011). It seeks to address and challenge the low participation of disadvantaged young people in society, and the generalised lack of political and social awareness and engagement in actions to promote public policies targeted at young people from poor neighbourhoods and urban peripheries. Other problems to be tackled include corruption, lack of housing, employment, precarious health and education. CCJ will work with young people from groups which are part of existing Catholic social networks and popular movements, community associations and the Catholic Youth Pastoral. 
The project aims to achieve 3 main outcomes: 1) New youth leaderships trained and strengthened; 2) Increased self esteem, awareness and organisational capacity of young people at local and national level for critical conscience and social involvement to defend their social rights and promote youth public policies; 3) Increased engagement, mobilisation and participation of young people (who live in favelas and poor areas of the city) in civil society and community initiatives to reduce young people&apos;s vulnerability.</narrative>
  </description>
